he was born into poverty but john hume  delivered what money couldn't buy  peace in northern ireland engaging in  secret talks with jerry adams  was the political gamble of his life he  was singularly against the ira  let's be clear about that unto his great  credit  that when the news broke about a meeting  with me  and he was the victim of a a tsunami of  abuse  and of vilification that he stuck with  it  over time he persuaded the irish  government that the gun could be taken  out of politics  and when he brought the british  government on board it was the beginning  of a peace process that would end with  the good friday agreement  john hume genuinely was a political  titan  i mean his contribution to peace in  northern ireland was extraordinary i  don't think we would ever  have really got the peace process going  and  implemented if he hadn't been there  offering help and advice  his reaching out to his unionist  neighbours had paid off  and in 1998 john hume and david trimble  were awarded the nobel prize for peace i  want to see ireland  as an example to men and women  everywhere  of what can be achieved by living for  ideals  rather than fighting or dying for them  bloody sunday when british soldiers shot  14 people dead in his native london  dairy had a profound impact on john hume  committed to the pursuit of irish unity  by entirely peaceful means  he co-founded the sdlp and won  international acclaim for his  peacemaking  but his heart was never far from home  john hume guided this city through some  of its darkest  days and the people here never forgot  that especially when he later found  himself  living with dementia they'd often meet  him walking alongside the river  and journey with him to ensure he  arrived home safely  john dined in the white house he spoke  in europe he spoke in french in the  european parliament he was  lauded all across the world but he was  never  as happy as when he was in derry  meeting dairy people speaking to dairy  people standing up  for the people of this city no matter  where he went he talked about derry  bill clinton who had become a close  personal friend  described john hume as the martin luther  king of northern ireland  [Music]  the man who refused to give up until his  dream of peace  became reality david blevins sky news  in derry
 

